  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Consider a tree with NNN nodes, rooted at node 111.\n\nThe value of the ithi^{th}ith node (1≤i≤N)(1 \\leq i \\leq N)(1≤i≤N) is denoted by AiA_iAi​.\n\nChef defines the function MEX(u,v)MEX(u, v)MEX(u,v) as follows:\n\nLet BBB denote the set of **all** the values of nodes that lie in the **shortest path** from uuu to vvv (including both uuu and vvv). Then, MEX(u,v)MEX(u, v)MEX(u,v) denotes the MEX of the set BBB.\n\nFind the **maximum** value of MEX(1,i)MEX(1, i)MEX(1,i), where 1≤i≤N1 \\leq i \\leq N1≤i≤N.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input contains a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases. The description of the TTT test cases follows.\nThe first line of each test case contains a single integer NNN - the number of nodes in the tree.\nThe second line of each test case contains NNN space separated integers A1,A2,...,ANA_1, A_2,..., A_NA1​,A2​,...,AN​. AiA_iAi​ represents the value of the ithi^{th}ith node.\nThe following N−1N-1N−1 lines contain two space-separated integers XXX and YYY, denoting that there exists an edge between the nodes XXX and YYY.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output in a single line, the maximum value of MEX(1,i)MEX(1, i)MEX(1,i) where 1≤i≤N1 \\leq i \\leq N1≤i≤N.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1041 \\leq T \\leq 10^41≤T≤104",
      "1≤N≤1051 \\leq N \\leq 10^51≤N≤105",
      "0≤Ai≤N0 \\leq A_i \\leq N0≤Ai​≤N",
      "1≤X,Y≤N1 \\leq X, Y \\leq N1≤X,Y≤N",
      "Sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 3⋅1053 \\cdot 10^53⋅105."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
